Debian Apache Arrow libraries for Qore
======================================

Copyright 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

Prepare with tools/prepare-debian-backports.py --suite trixie apache-arrow.
The manifest pins the Apache 25.0.1 release and independent arrow-testing,
parquet-testing and xsimd components by HTTPS URL and SHA-256. All downloads
and verification happen before the source package is built. Native builds
run without network access, using the declared Debian build dependencies.

The package includes shared Arrow, compute, Acero, dataset, Flight, Flight SQL
and Parquet libraries and their development packages. CSV, JSON, IPC,
filesystems, supported compression codecs and Parquet encryption are enabled.
CUDA, Gandiva, Substrait, ORC, HDFS, cloud storage backends, GLib bindings and
command-line utilities are not included. PyArrow is a separate source package.

The pinned xsimd headers are exposed through a private build-tree CMake package.
No xsimd library or headers are installed, and consumers need no private xsimd
path. Security updates to these headers require rebuilding Arrow. Preserve
all orig source components alongside the packages. Upstream LICENSE.txt and
NOTICE.txt and xsimd's license are installed with every binary package; the
complete fixture and third-party license records remain in debian/copyright.

The upstream runtime-SSE4.2 fix keeps amd64 code at the baseline instruction
set while dispatching optimized kernels on capable CPUs. The patch retains
upstream's regression checks and arm64 NEON handling. Native qualification
must exercise the full configured CTest suite, installed SDK consumers,
package lifecycle, detached debug symbols, hardening and reproducibility on
both amd64 and arm64 before repository publication. tzdata-legacy supplies
historical zone aliases and locales-all enables the locale-dependent tests.
Tests run unprivileged and require no external services.
